{
	"Name": "Search - LLM - Semantic - Sensitive Data and PII Disclosure [table]",
	"Description": "Finds prompts that appear to be pasting regulated or customer data into a model. Useful for showing where an approved-use policy is being ignored.\n\nRequires embeddings on the entries (vector preprocessor on the LLM listener) and an embedding model configured in the webserver's [AI] section. Without both, this query returns nothing. Tune sensitivity with the LLM_SEMANTIC_THRESHOLD config macro rather than editing the query.\n\n`embeddings` is an intrinsic enumerated value, so it is declared on the intrinsic extraction module alongside everything else the query needs; the semantic module cannot see it otherwise.",
	"GUID": "8db9ab07-25e1-5599-b708-5828c91233ef",
